      "statement_sha256": "48934ecb301f858b8332eea15194ff42a119fd7c1c7a7402089467a4994b3dd7",
      "text": "For every N > 0, all real vectors a, b indexed by Fin N with every a_i > 0, and every real X: (1) sum_i br(lamStar)_i = X, where br(lam)_i = b_i - lam/a_i and lamStar = (sum_i b_i - X)/(sum_i 1/a_i); and (2) for every y with sum_i y_i = X, J(xStar) <= J(y), where J(x) = sum_i (a_i/2)(x_i - b_i)^2 and xStar_i = br(lamStar)_i.",
      "trivial": false
    },
    "C2": {
      "kind": "conjecture",
      "label": "ASSUMED",
      "reason": "conjecture",
      "text": "Observation from local Lean checks, not a sealed claim: part (2) of P2.Harmonization holds without the hypothesis N > 0 (for N = 0 both dissipations are the empty sum 0), whereas it fails if a curvature may be zero: with N = 2, a = (0,1), b = (0,0), X = 1, Lean's 1/0 = 0 convention gives xStar = (0,1) with J = 1/2, while the feasible y = (1,0) has J = 0."
    }
